EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
       The following example sets the read‐only flag  on  the  filesystem  in‐
       stance referenced by the mount object attached at _/_t_m_p.

           int fsfd = fspick(AT_FDCWD, "/tmp", FSPICK_CLOEXEC);
           fsconfig(fsfd, FSCONFIG_SET_FLAG, "ro", NULL, 0);
           fsconfig(fsfd, FSCONFIG_CMD_RECONFIGURE, NULL, NULL, 0);

       The above procedure is roughly equivalent to the following mount opera‐
       tion using mmoouunntt(2):

           mount(NULL, "/tmp", NULL, MS_REMOUNT | MS_RDONLY, NULL);

       With  the  notable caveat that in this example, mmoouunntt(2) will clear all
       other filesystem parameters (such as MMSS__DDIIRRSSYYNNCC or MMSS__SSYYNNCCHHRROONNOOUUSS); ffss‐‐
       ccoonnffiigg(2) will only modify the rroo parameter.

